This TachyonikProxy installation was made from a .deb or .rpm package, so your
system package manager owns it. Built-in auto-update is disabled here: it would
write over files dpkg/rpm track, leaving the package database describing a
version that is no longer on disk — and the next package upgrade would silently
undo it.

To upgrade, re-run the installer, which fetches the current package:

    curl -fsSL https://tachyonik.com/download/proxy/install-tachyonikproxy.sh | sudo sh

Or download the current .deb/.rpm from https://tachyonik.com/download/proxy/ and
install it with your package manager.

Auto-update applies to the standalone (.tar.gz) installation instead.
